[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Resource_w76o3"]
script = ExtResource("5_qv0b1")
markedup_text = "Harvest the seeds."
requirement = SubResource("Resource_fugsy")
outcome = SubResource("Resource_h54f5")
markedup_result_text = "The flowers are the size of a person's head, heavy with pollen.

The settlers carefully collect the seeds, wondering if they will grow so huge in other soils, or if this was a singular quirk of this specific place.

Either way, the potential is now stored in a pouch, waiting for a new home."

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Resource_41fiy"]
script = ExtResource("16_jigde")
delta = -5
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://c23hf0l6630h1"

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Resource_svhlh"]
script = ExtResource("5_qv0b1")
markedup_text = "Cook a feast for the whole settlement."
outcome = SubResource("Resource_41fiy")
markedup_result_text = "The stems are chopped like timber and boiled in the largest cauldrons available.

The expectations are high, but the results are... educational. A settler describes it as similar to chewing on warm rope, and the bitterness lingers in the mouth long after the meal is finished.

\"Well,\" the cook sighs, dumping the leftovers. \"At least we know why the rodents didn't eat it.\""

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Resource_7ivte"]
script = ExtResource("3_8r7oa")
markedup_text = "The butterbur plants were meant to be a modest patch for cough medicine. Something in the soil disagreed with that plan, though.

The stems have surged to the height of a house, and the leaves are now vast green parasols, casting the entire garden in deep, cool shade.

The herbalist measures a stem and notes that the hollow core could fit a kettle. \"Is it a miracle of vitality,\" she wonders, \"or a very large mistake?\""
background_image = SubResource("Resource_qv0b1")
background_credit = ExtResource("5_i3w4q")
choices = Array[ExtResource("5_qv0b1")]([SubResource("Resource_npbag"), SubResource("Resource_jbdhy"), SubResource("Resource_w76o3")])
exit_choice = SubResource("Resource_svhlh")

